# TEMPORARY — batch integration only, removed before the wave is closed.
#
# The branches of a wave are developed in parallel worktrees and each one adds a
# handful of lines to the same spine files (a container property, a ProfileView
# row, a RootView route, a client method). Those additions land on the same
# anchors, so a plain three-way merge reports a conflict for what is really
# "keep both". The `union` driver does exactly that.
#
# Line-oriented, therefore only safe because every branch was required to keep
# its spine edits additive and minimal: a rename or a rework on both sides would
# concatenate nonsense. Measured: it concatenates exactly where two branches
# touch the SAME line (four sites in P2/P3). The build gate catches that in
# seconds; the suite on the integrated tree catches what compiles but lies.
